@comment{
  XBSTRXCT shared bibliography (BibTeX / BibLaTeX).
  Cite an entry in any page by its key in square brackets, with an at-sign before the key;
  see content/about/authoring.md. Edit by hand or export from a reference manager
  (e.g. Zotero + Better BibTeX, "Keep updated"). Seed entries: works already cited in the essays.
  Parser limits: no at-signs inside comments, and no bare percent-sign comment lines.
  A publisher containing "and" needs double braces, e.g. {{Williams and Norgate}}.
  Links: each entry has one url or doi, shown as a link on the title (quartz/plugins/abstraction/linkReferences.ts).
  Prefer a free full text (Gutenberg, Wikisource, archive.org, author or publisher), then a DOI, then Google Books.
  Publisher DOIs replaced by free copies: shannon1948mathematical 10.1002/j.1538-7305.1948.tb01338.x,
  turing1936computable 10.1112/plms/s2-42.1.230.
  Linked edition differs from the cited one: llull1501ars (1517 Lyon edition), whitehead1927principia
  (first edition, vol. 1, 1910), leibniz1981new (1996 revised edition).
}

